msgstr ""

#: ../../../scripting/custom_targets.rst:45
msgid "``AddCustomTarget`` arguments:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../scripting/custom_targets.rst:0
msgid "name"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../scripting/custom_targets.rst:48
msgid ""
"A name of target. ASCII chars (a-z, 0-9, _, -) are recommended. Good names "
"are \"gen_headers\", \"program_bitstream\", etc."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../scripting/custom_targets.rst:0
msgid "dependencies"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../scripting/custom_targets.rst:52
msgid ""
"A list of dependencies that should be built BEFORE target will be launched. "
"It is possible pass multiple dependencies as a Python list ``[\"dep1\", "
"dep_target_2]``. If a target does not have dependencies, ``None`` should be "
"passed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../scripting/custom_targets.rst:0
msgid "actions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../scripting/custom_targets.rst:57
msgid ""
"A list of actions to call on a target. It is possible to pass multiple "
"actions as a Python list ``[\"python --version\", my_calback]``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../scripting/custom_targets.rst:0
msgid "title"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../scripting/custom_targets.rst:61
msgid ""
"A title of a target. It will be printed when using :ref:`piocore` or :ref:"
"`pioide`. We recommend to keep a title very short, 1-2 words."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../scripting/custom_targets.rst:0
msgid "description"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../scripting/custom_targets.rst:65
msgid ""
"The same as a ``title`` argument but allows you to provide detailed "
"explanation what target does."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../scripting/custom_targets.rst:0
msgid "always_build"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../scripting/custom_targets.rst:69
msgid ""
"If there are declared ``dependencies`` and they are already built, this "
"target will not be called if ``always_build=False``. A default value is "
"``always_build=True`` and means always building/calling target."
msgstr ""

